Query 2: Compound Join Condition
• write a query that produces the following output displaying customers with an actor name
• tables: customer, actor
• sort by customer name
 *************************************************************/
 SELECT CONCAT(a.last_name, ', ', a.first_name) as customer_name, 
 CONCAT(a.last_name, ', ', a.first_name) as actor_name
 FROM actor a JOIN customer c
 ON a.last_name = c.last_name
 AND a.first_name = c.first_name;
/***********************************************************
Query 3: Self-Join
• write a query that produces the following output for customers with the same first name
• tables: customer
• sort by first name and last name
*****************************************************/
Select c1.customer_id, c1.store_id, c1.first_name, c1.last_name
From customer c1 JOIN customer c2
On c1.first_name = c2.first_name and c1.last_name <> c2.last_name
Order By c1.first_name, c1.last_name ASC;
/******************************************************
Query 4: More than two tables
• Write a query that produces the following output displaying the staff’s address
• tables: staff, address, city, country
• sort by last name and first name
********************************************/
SELECT staff_id, CONCAT(s.last_name, ' , ', s.first_name) AS staff_name, email, store_id, a.district, city, country
FROM staff s
	JOIN address a
		ON s.address_id = a.address_id
	JOIN city c1
		ON a.city_id = c1.city_id
	JOIN country c2
		ON c1.country_id = c2.country_id
/************************************************************
Query 5: Implicit Inner Join
• Convert query 4 from an explicit join to an implicit join.
• Result set will be the same.
NOTE: The following StackOverflow explains why you should NOT to use implicit (comma JOIN) syntax
****************************************************************/
SELECT s.staff_id,
       CONCAT(s.last_name, ' , ', s.first_name) AS staff_name, s.email, s.store_id, a.district, c1.city, c2.country
FROM staff s, address a, city c1, country c2
WHERE s.address_id = a.address_id
  AND a.city_id = c1.city_id
  AND c1.country_id = c2.country_id;
